After marking a low of 22,217, the benchmark index Nifty witnessed a pullback of more than 550 points. However, the recovery lacked sustainability, and the index resumed its downward trajectory on Wednesday.
Technically, the index continues to trade below its key moving averages, indicating that the broader trend remains weak. That said, the gap between the 20-day EMA and the closing price has narrowed considerably, suggesting a mean reversion following the recent sharp correction. Momentum indicators and oscillators continue to reflect bearish undertones, while the daily RSI remains in the super bearish zone as per the RSI range shift framework.
Going forward, the 22,800-22,850 zone is likely to act as a crucial resistance area. A sustained move above 22,850 could extend the pullback towards the 23,100 mark. On the downside, the 22,450-22,400 zone remains an important support area, and any breach of this zone may invite renewed selling pressure.
